  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Humanitarian Response to the Mixed Flows Crossing the Darien Jungle</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide life-saving humanitarian assistance to vulnerable migrants in transit or at the temporary Migrant Reception Station (ETRMs) in the Darien or in the remote communities in the Comarca Embera Wounaan. This IOM project conducts Camp Coordination and Camp Management activities at the ETRMs, needs assessment and refer urgent populations&#x2019; needs to relevant services, facilitates refresher sessions for humanitarian staff and government partners, provides access to food, health, essential Non-Food Items, protection assistance and improves emergency shelter conditions. The project provides life-saving assistance to 80,000 individuals, including 43,200 men, 20,800 women, 16,00 children, and including 240 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
